      space(),

      h2("4.2 Key Analytical Notes on the Probability Distribution"),
      p("The combined probability of conclusions involving some degree of non-public institutional knowledge or active managed operation (B + C) is 70%. The conventional explanation (A + D) accounts for 30% of the probability mass. This distribution reflects honest weighing of the evidence rather than default assignment of majority probability to the conventional explanation."),
      p("Conclusions C's test and trigger components were initially assessed separately before the analytical observation that testing a managed injection system and deploying it as a trigger are sequential phases of one operation rather than distinct conclusions. Any successful capability test validates the deployment methodology. Separating them artificially inflates the apparent probability of capability-testing without deployment intent, which is not a coherent standalone conclusion."),
      p("The 25% assigned to natural explanation reflects real evidentiary support: the USGS characterization is genuine, the 1996-2004 precedent is real, and the broad spatial distribution of seismicity is not inconsistent with natural fluid diffusion. These items prevent the natural explanation from being dismissed. They do not outweigh the items against it."),

      space(),
