      p("The following findings would significantly alter the probability assessment. UUSS providing the 2025-2026 seismic catalog data in response to inquiry — if the data shows normal pattern consistent with prior natural episodes, probability shifts toward natural explanation. If the data shows anomalous spatial or depth characteristics inconsistent with natural process, probability shifts toward managed injection. If UUSS does not respond or claims the data is unavailable, the non-response itself is evidence consistent with institutional sensitivity around the anomalous period."),
      p("Equipment procurement records for the 2023 Norris Geyser Basin installation obtainable through FOIA — specifically the detailed equipment manifest for the subsurface borehole components — would establish whether injection-capable infrastructure was installed alongside monitoring equipment. Standard monitoring borehole instruments and injection wellhead equipment are physically distinct and would appear differently in procurement records."),
      p("Independent seismic analysis of the November 2025 swarm by a geophysicist without institutional connection to USGS, UUSS, or EarthScope Consortium — applying the spatial clustering methodology from the Science Advances July 2025 paper on Yellowstone swarm dynamics — would provide independent assessment of whether the swarm characteristics are consistent with natural fluid diffusion or distributed injection origin."),
